# WordPress permalinks, for an install that lives at /blog.
#
# 🔴 RewriteBase and the fallback path BOTH carry the /blog prefix. This is the
# one file where the prefix has to be written out literally, because Apache
# resolves these against the URL space the browser asked for, not against the
# document root. Drop the prefix from either line and the homepage keeps
# working while every post URL 404s.
#
# Baked into the image so a fresh container has working permalinks before anyone
# opens wp-admin. WordPress will rewrite this file if permalinks are re-saved;
# it regenerates exactly these lines, so that is harmless.

# BEGIN WordPress
<IfModule mod_rewrite.c>
RewriteEngine On
RewriteBase /blog/
RewriteRule ^index\.php$ - [L]
RewriteCond %{REQUEST_FILENAME} !-f
RewriteCond %{REQUEST_FILENAME} !-d
RewriteRule . /blog/index.php [L]
</IfModule>
# END WordPress
